### Only an 'admin' may create a region — the descriptor gives `regions` no other create rule
# @name CreateNorthRegion
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/regions
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "NORTH",
  "name": "Northern region"
}

### A second region, so a filter over `region_id` has something to discriminate
# @name CreateCentralRegion
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/regions
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "CENTRAL",
  "name": "Central region"
}

### A dispatcher may not create one: `regions.create` names 'admin' and nothing else
# @name DispatcherCannotCreateRegion
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [403]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/regions
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "WEST",
  "name": "Western region"
}
